On Wed, 22 May 96 14:42:12 MDT, my original question was:

> Hello,
> 	I've had no problems running Netscape 2.0 on our Alphas, but
> when I recently tried to install Netscape 3.0, it gives a lot of error
> messages and never starts up. The error messages are as follows:
> 
> netscape3_0: X Error of failed request:  BadWindow (invalid Window parameter)
>   Major opcode of failed request:  61 (X_ClearArea)
>   Resource id in failed request:  0x4400024
>   Serial number of failed request:  324
>   Current serial number in output stream:  1048
> 
> The opcodes of the errors are different, but the rest is the same.
> xdpyinfo gives me the following for the default visual id:
>   visual:
>     visual id:    0x25
>     class:    PseudoColor
>     depth:    8 planes
>     size of colormap:    256 entries
>     red, green, blue masks:    0x0, 0x0, 0x0
>     significant bits in color specification:    8 bits
> 
> Also, this is a ZLXp-L2 graphics controller (sizer -gt).

There were a few responses. Seems like Netscape 3.0 doesn't know how to
handle (yet?) when the default visual is 8 planes on a 24 plane display.
The solutions are two:
a) Change default visual to 24 planes (which I can't do for other
reasons)
b) Run netscape as:    netscape -visual PseudoColor

Option (b) works great for me now!

