    Fellow OSF Managers,
    
    We have (had) a 2100/275 with two 4/275 processors running DU 
    3.2D-1.  We are using AdvFS over top of an HSZ40 with two logical 
    disks (2 domains, 1 fileset, 2 filesets).  We are using this 
    system to run Oracle, SAS, and NetSite.
    
    The errors we have had have almost all been simple_lock errors.  
    We applied the complete patch set from Digital Support and this 
    seemed to increase the frequency of the crashes from 1 every few 
    days to one every few hours.  It also changed the panic string 
    from "simple_lock: time limit exceeded" to "simple_lock: 
    unitialized lock".
    
    We have currently switched back to a single CPU system and are not 
    having any crashes, but we would like to be able to run SMP.  Is 
    anyone out there running a similar system?  Does anyone know what 
    the problem could be?  Digital support has not been terribly 
    helpful with this one (ongoing problems since Feb).
    
    Regards,
    Mandell Degerness
