Subject: SUMMARY: SWXCR RAID and RZ29
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076332421603

Summary:

My original posting was:
> 
> Hi managers!
> 
> I have only a short question: In the booklet to the SWXCR EISA-RAID =3D
> controller in our 2100 is mentioned, that only RZ28 disks can be used, =
=3D
> but RZ29 were not know at this time at all. Does someone know if this =
is =3D
> still valid? And when I expand, can I use different disks (of the same =
=3D
> size) or different revision-levels of the RZ28?

The answer was, that it is possible and qualified by DEC to use RZ29 disk =
with SWXCR RAID. Minimum fimware rev. 0014 of the disks and newest for =
the SWXCR. But you have to pay attention to the heat (cooling and 2nd =
power supply necessary in 2100).

It is even possible to mix disks (RZ28 RZ29 ..), but when using in one =
logical drive you loose lots of space. Tip: Only use one kind of disks in =
one logical drive to avoid trouble.

     Here's an example (a particulary wasteful one at that):
         RAID-5 with 4 RZ29s and 1 RZ26 =3D 4GB usable space
     Better off to do:
         1 RZ26 JBOD   =3D  1 GB
       + 4 RZ29 RAID-5 =3D 12 GB

Robert

