Thanks once again for the help!

Problem:  too much of a stiped volume was reserved for root (default is 10%)
and I couldn't figure out how to reclaim some of it.  dxlsm doesn't have a way
(that I could find in the fine manauls) and newfs -m wouldn't work...

Solution:  after unmounting the logical volume, tunefs -m VALUE /dev/...

I used VALUE=2 and all is COOL!!!

