From tru64-unix-managers  Mon May 27 13:37:15 1996
From: "Richard A. Muirden" <richard () rmit ! EDU ! AU>
Date: Mon, 27 May 1996 13:37:15 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: rptys !! - SOLVED!! :)
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076332421530

I asked about rptys. The speedy and marvelous response came from 
Miochael Long <MLONG@karmax.com>:

--
Hi Richard,

In Dec UNIX 3.2C rpty's were taken out of the static kernel parmaters and   
put into sysconfig, so that you don't have to rebuild the kernel each   
time you increase rpty's.  This important piece of information is buried   
somewhere in the release notes, but you'll have to look hard to find it!

You should create the following entry in /etc/sysconfigtab.  Tabs instead   
of spaces are important as this is a stanza compliant file:

pts:
        nptys=1500


Please note that the entry is nptys and not rptys.  You should remove the   
rpty entry from your config file before your next kernel rebuild.

Hope this helps,

Michael Long.
Karmax Heavy Stamping  
--

Thank you Michael, and to Henk who just mailed. works purrfectly now.
Nice of Digital to make that obvious in their release notes!!! :)

