I got only one response in the day from Linda; thanks, Linda. She
confirmed that the standard print would only print one copy, but that
she had a hp-filter that fixed this problem. She was kind enough to send
me the filter uuencoded. I won't get a chance to try this till May 28,
but I am expecting that this will solve my problem.

Attached is Linda's message.

regards, kris.

Dear Kris!


Your so right. It doesn't work that way.

But there is a hp-filter that does the job.
We've got it from our local DEC representation.

It is call hpnpf and the printcap looks likes this:

pr13u:\
        :if=/usr/lbin/pr13u.of:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lp13uerr:\
        :lp=/dev/null:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd13u:\
        :xf=/usr/lbin/xf:

The /usr/lbin/pr13u.of looks like this

! /usr/bin/csh -f
/usr/lbin/hpnpf -x dr13.por.bka -N
