Merci!, danke!, tak!, and thanks! to all of the people that responded so
quickly!

The way to add a new hard disk is to:

1. cd /dev
2. ./MAKEDEV /dev/rz#  (# = scsi id + 8)
3. disklabel -wr /dev/rrz#c FOO  (FOO = quantum or /dev/rrz#c or whatever)
4. newfs /dev/rrz#c

(It worked for me at least)

If anyone notices any errors above, or a way to format _all_ of the new disk at
one go (instead of rrz#a, rrz#b, rrz#c,...) please let me know.

Thanks again,
Rich

