My question was related to information about /usr/field executables.
Many thanks to:

Chris Ruffieux
Seela (seela.balkissoon@sheridan.on.ca)

Seela suggested me to check the complementary CD (no luck there)
Chris sent these useful information:

===================================================
Javier,

    here is some info.  i am not sure where we picked it up so
    i wouldn't just post it in your summary before verifying it.

    chris


    /usr/field/advscan

    This command determines which partitions on a disk are part of
    an AdvFS file domain.  It's extremely useful in rebuilding the
    /etc/fdmns directory.  This is the directory that contains info
    about the AdvFS file domains on a system.  

    Example:  % /usr/field/advscan rz1

    /usr/field/vchkdir

    This is an AdvFS directory structure checker and fixer.  It verifies
    that the directory structure is correct and that all directory 
    entries have a valid file (tag) and that all files (tags) have a
    directory entry.

    Example:  % /usr/field/vchkdir /usr

    /usr/field/msfsck

    msfsck is the AdvFS bitfile-subsystem metadata structure checker.
    It verifies low-level meta-structures.  Note, when using this
    command you must be in the same directory as the .tags file.
    This is the mount point for the fileset.

    Example: % /usr/field/msfsck usr_domain usr
===============================================

Thanks again

