hosts - (most suggested going through something like ASE) - it seems
like you can do it, but probably don't want to unless you can control
access or live with the consequences.  The question was raised as a
crude (but creative) way to address common storage for systems on two
different networks (in front of and behind a firewall) where the main
concern is not the passing of data, but the isolation of systems.

thanks to all those who responded.  I appreciate your taking the time
to answer!

