From tru64-unix-managers  Thu May 02 19:39:00 1996
From: Ry Jones <RJONES () hbsi ! com>
Date: Thu, 02 May 1996 19:39:00 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: SOLUTION: 8200 + Oracle == CRASH
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076332421165


The solution was this:
1) My HSZ40B's were PROM REV 2.50. They were missing 4 bug fixes on 2.5,   
and PROM 2.7 was out. These were upgraded.
2) I was running 3.2C. I upgraded to 3.2D. These were the most immediate   
issue.

I got replies from Kurt Carlson, Jari Tavi, and Vipin Gokhale.

The issue was:
Oracle + 8200, under light loads, would cause pciaerror: cpu8: panic.

2 patches for this crash were available from DEC, but the preferred   
method of fixing it was to upgrade to 3.2D.

Sorry for being so late in posting this summary, but we only recently   
signed off on the fix. For a while it looked like we were going to   
replace the IOM and the CPU's, but that didn't happen.
Ry
